---
// ============================================================================
// LEGAL — REVIEW WITH YOUR OWN ATTORNEY BEFORE LAUNCH.
// This is generic, plain-language boilerplate written for a California
// home-services business. It is NOT legal advice and it has not been reviewed
// by a lawyer. Before this site goes live, have a California attorney review
// and amend it so that it matches the business's actual written contract,
// deposit and cancellation terms, warranty periods, limitation-of-liability
// wording, CSLB home-improvement contract requirements and the mandatory
// three-day right-to-cancel notice. Update the "lastUpdated" date whenever
// the text changes.
// ============================================================================
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../data/schema';

const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { name: 'Terms of Service', href: '/terms' },
];

const schema = [breadcrumbSchema(crumbs)];
const lastUpdated = 'October 31, 2026';
---
<Base
  title="Terms of Service | Water Heater Repair Rocklin, CA"
  description="The terms that apply to using this website and to water heater work carried out by our Rocklin, CA company — estimates, pricing, warranty and liability."
  path="/terms"
  schema={schema}
  noindex={false}
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="note">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <p>
        These terms cover two things: using this website, and hiring {site.legalName} to work on your
        water heater. By using the site or booking work with us, you agree to them. Where a signed
        written contract or work order for a specific job says something different, that document wins.
      </p>

      <h2>About Us</h2>
      <p>
        {site.legalName !== site.name ? `${site.legalName}, trading as ${site.name}` : site.name}, {site.address.street},
        {site.address.city}, {site.address.region} {site.address.postalCode}. Phone
        <a href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phone}</a>, email
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Using This Website</h2>
      <p>
        The content here is general information about water heaters and our services. It is not a
        diagnosis of your equipment and it is not an offer of a fixed price. Prices, ranges and
        timescales shown on this site are typical figures for the Rocklin area and are illustrative
        only — your actual price comes from an estimate given to you for your specific unit and
        property. We may change the content of this site at any time without notice.
      </p>
      <p>
        Please do not use this site to attempt unauthorised access, to scrape it at a volume that
        disrupts it, or to copy its text and images for another business. The text, images, logo and
        layout belong to us or our licensors.
      </p>

      <h2>Safety Information Is Not a Substitute for a Technician</h2>
      <p>
        Some pages describe steps such as closing a cold inlet valve or switching off a breaker. Those
        are included to help you limit damage while you wait for us. Water heaters involve gas,
        electricity, pressurised water and scalding temperatures. If you choose to work on your own
        equipment you do so at your own risk, and we accept no responsibility for the outcome. If you
        ever smell gas, leave the building and call your gas utility from outside before calling us.
      </p>

      <h2>Estimates and Pricing</h2>
      <p>
        We quote a diagnostic or service-call fee before we come out. On site we diagnose the fault and
        give you a written price for the work. No work starts until you approve that price. If you
        approve the repair, the diagnostic fee is credited against it.
      </p>
      <p>
        An estimate assumes normal access and the conditions we could see at the time. If hidden
        conditions appear once panels come off or a unit is drained — corroded piping, unsafe venting,
        an undersized gas line, electrical faults, a missing pan or code upgrades required to pass
        inspection — we will stop, explain, and give you a revised written price for your approval
        before continuing. Estimates are valid for 30 days unless stated otherwise.
      </p>

      <h2>Scheduling, Access and Cancellation</h2>
      <p>
        Arrival windows are our best estimate and can move when an emergency call comes in; we will
        tell you if that happens. You agree to give us safe, clear access to the water heater and to
        secure pets during the visit. If we cannot access the unit, or nobody is home at the agreed
        time, we may charge the service-call fee. Please give us as much notice as you can if you need
        to cancel or reschedule.
      </p>

      <h2>Payment</h2>
      <p>
        Payment is due on completion of the work unless we have agreed otherwise in writing. Larger
        replacement jobs may require a deposit, which will be set out in the written contract for that
        job and will comply with California limits on contractor deposits. Equipment we supply remains
        our property until it has been paid for in full.
      </p>

      <h2>Permits and Code Compliance</h2>
      <p>
        Water heater replacement in California normally requires a permit and an inspection. Where we replace a
        unit we pull the permit and install to current code, including seismic strapping, correct
        relief-valve discharge, drain pan and expansion tank where required. If you ask us to carry out
        work that would not meet code, we will decline it.
      </p>

      <h2>Warranty</h2>
      <p>
        Our workmanship is guaranteed. If something we repaired or installed fails because of how we
        did the work, tell us and we will come back and put it right at no charge for the labor.
        Equipment and parts carry the manufacturer's own warranty, and the manufacturer's terms —
        including any requirement that the unit be properly maintained — govern those claims. We will
        help you make a claim and provide our records.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our guarantee does not cover faults caused by misuse, freezing, water quality, work by others,
        power or gas supply problems, sediment or scale damage on a unit that has not been maintained,
        or an existing unit or component we advised you to replace and you chose to keep.
      </p>

      <h2>Pre-Existing Conditions and Water Damage</h2>
      <p>
        We are frequently called to equipment that is already leaking or already failed. We are not
        responsible for damage that existed before we arrived, for damage caused by a failure that was
        already in progress, or for consequential damage such as loss of use, mold remediation or
        damaged belongings, except to the extent it was caused by our own negligence.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of Liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by California law, our total liability arising out of any job is
        limited to the amount you paid us for that job, and we are not liable for indirect, incidental
        or consequential losses. Nothing in these terms limits any liability that cannot lawfully be
        limited, and nothing here removes your rights under the California home improvement contract
        rules, including your right to cancel within the statutory period where it applies.
      </p>

      <h2>Complaints</h2>
      <p>
        If something is wrong, call us first — most issues are fixed by sending a technician back. Email
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> or call
        <a href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phone}</a>. California licensed contractors are also subject to
        the oversight of the {site.license.authority}, and you may contact that body about a licensed
        contractor at any time.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing Law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of the State of California, and any dispute will be heard
        in the courts serving Placer County, California.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms; the date at the top shows when they last changed. The version in
        force is the one published when you book your work.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms can go to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> or
        <a href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phone}</a>. See also our
        <a href="/privacy-policy">privacy policy</a> and <a href="/contact-us">contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
